From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:15:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] ipa: softisp: af: Add the autofocus controls

The software ISP autofocus runs continuously over the whole statistics
window, with no way for an application to control it, and runs on the
frames without statistics too, measuring the same frame four times.

Run the AfAlgorithm on new statistics only, and offer its controls,
AfMode, AfTrigger, AfPause and LensPosition, and AfMetering and
AfWindows on top. Report AfState, AfPauseState and LensPosition in the
metadata.

The variance is the contrast of the focus zones normalised to their
brightness. AfMeteringAuto measures the centre quarter of the image;
AfMeteringWindows weighs the zones by the area of the AfWindows they
hold. To map the windows, which are in sensor coordinates, to the zones
the IPA gets the ScalerCrop of the output at configure time.

The controls are only offered with a focus lens. As the camera controls
are known before the camera is configured, pass the lens controls to the
IPA at init time too.

Reported-by: Jayden Milne <me@jayd.ml>
Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
